# Chroma library, modern Earth: SHAPE MOMENTS for the ladder shapes cause and faith (v25 prep draft, 10-23).
# Syntax: header of build.py, plus the v25 keys shape:, kind:, rungs:, fork: (moments) and aim:, cost: (options),
# aims-shape.md section 4. Pours into chroma-library/earth_shape_moments-*.lib (POUR-NOTES.md). Nothing built or run.
# Every moment: the five one-colour ways and one full cross cycle (s1 W>U U>B B>R R>G G>W, s2 W>B U>R B>G R>W G>U).
# cause rungs: 0 caring, 1 joining, 2 organising, 3 leading, 4 a change that lasts. Its "contest" is a test: a vote, a
#   hearing, a deadline, the big night ({aim.contest} names it). Fields: the street, justice, the public's business,
#   the rules, answering to no one, living by one's own rules, the underdog, the wild places, what is right, the parties.
# faith rungs: 0 seeking, 1 belonging, 2 serving, 3 guiding, 4 a teacher remembered. Its "contest" is a rite or a trial
#   of faith. Fields: finding what is true, the old texts, music in worship, a congregation for life, living in balance,
#   the packs' faith-leader calling. Words never name a faith and never argue for or against belief.
# All moments are 12 and over (cause and faith have no child moments, SHAPES.md).

# ================================================================ CAUSE

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- cause, practice, rungs 0 1 (cycle s1)

== the ordinary weeknight at {aim.place}
tier: life event
shape: cause
kind: practice
rungs: 0 1
fork:
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 12-85
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: joy
life: community, friends
horizon: week
roles: friend, mentor, rival, elder
earth: an ordinary weeknight of {aim.doing}: a few people, a kettle and a list of jobs nobody wants
tribal: an evening by the fire where the few who care about {aim.thing} talk it through
magic: an evening in the guild's back room where the few who care about {aim.thing} meet
scene: It is an ordinary weeknight at {aim.place}: six people, a kettle and a list of jobs nobody wants. {N} has been {aim.doing} for a few months now, and tonight {aim.person} looks round the room for a volunteer.
scene tribal: The fire is low and only a few have stayed to talk about {aim.thing}. {elder} looks round the circle for someone to take on the next small job.
scene magic: The guild's back room is cold and half empty, and the list of small jobs for {aim.thing} is long. {aim.person} looks up from it, at {N}.
- W | take the dullest job on the list and have it done by the next meeting | v: conformity, benevolence | aim: work | foot: mark kept your word | chance: 85
- U | read up on how others have gone about {aim.thing} before saying a word | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: work | foot: lesson others have tried this before | chance: 80
- B | offer to speak for the group next time, so people learn your name | v: power, achievement | aim: work | foot: means ties+.03 | chance: 65
- R | stay on after the meeting arguing about what the group should really do | v: stimulation, self-direction | aim: work | foot: person friend | chance: 75
- G | come when the week allows, and keep the other evenings for home | v: benevolence, security | aim: ease | foot: means time+.03 | chance: 90
- W>U | write down who does what, so nothing falls through the cracks | v: conformity, self-direction | aim: work | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 85
- U>B | work out which job would actually change something, and take that one | v: achievement, power | aim: work | foot: lesson the right job beats more jobs | chance: 70
- B>R | skip the list and start something of your own that the group can join | v: power, stimulation | aim: work | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 55
- R>G | leave the jobs for tonight and just get to know the people in the room | v: hedonism, benevolence | aim: ease | foot: means ties+.04 | chance: 85
- G>W | do the jobs nobody sees, and turn up again next week the same | v: benevolence, conformity | aim: work | foot: person regular | chance: 85
works: The job gets done, and someone at the next meeting notices without being told.
works: {N} walks home with the sense that a small thing moved, and it did.
fails: Half the room does not come back the week after, and the list is longer than ever.
fails: {N} meant to do it, and the week got in the way.

