scene tribal: {rival} speaks for {aim.thing} at another fire of the clan, in another way. The same families are hearing both, and growing tired of it.
scene magic: {rival} leads a circle of the guild that wants what {N} wants by other means, and courts the same patrons.
- W | propose one shared plan, with clear rules on who does what | v: conformity, universalism | aim: work | foot: door kept your word | chance: 60
- U | study what they do better, and borrow it openly | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: work | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 75
- B | outwork them until people come to your door first | v: power, achievement | aim: try | foot: person rival | chance: 55
- R | challenge them to a public debate about whose way works | v: stimulation, power | aim: try | foot: place gather.talk | chance: 50
- G | leave them the streets they already know, and keep to the old patch | v: security, tradition | aim: ease | foot: lesson there is room for both | chance: 85
- W>B | meet them in private and agree to split the work fairly | v: conformity, power | aim: work | foot: person go-between | chance: 60
- U>R | try the bold thing they keep talking about, before they do | v: self-direction, stimulation | aim: try | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 45
- B>G | win over their oldest supporters, one by one | v: power, tradition | aim: try | foot: person regular | chance: 50
- R>W | say publicly what they get right, and mean it | v: stimulation, universalism | aim: ease | foot: means ties+.04 | chance: 75
- G>U | invite them round, and find the one thing you both want most | v: benevolence, self-direction | aim: work | foot: person friend | chance: 65
works: The town ends up with two groups pulling the same way, and both are stronger for it.
works: {rival} gives ground on one point, and {N} gives on another.
fails: People tire of being asked twice, and some stop answering either group.
fails: The quarrel becomes the story, and {aim.thing} gets lost behind it.

